NUM-32: infiltrate only the ponded water left after evaporation

RunoffSolver::execute() charges evaporation to the ponded water first
(surfEvap = min(depth/dt, evapRate)) and then asks for the infiltration rate
with the full ponded depth, so infiltration can take water that has already
evaporated. When the two together use up the surface water the depth is set
to zero but both full volumes are booked, up to evap x dt of water that never
existed. Pass the depth left after evaporation to infilGetInfil() (the same
change as the 5.3.0 patch).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-32_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
index aa81dc7..89f08a1 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Runoff.cpp
@@ -454,7 +454,10 @@ void RunoffSolver::execute(SimulationContext& ctx, double dt, double evap_rate_i
                 }
 
                 infil_factor_used_[ui] = local_infil;
-                infil = infilGetInfil(ctx, i, precip, runon, depth, dt,
+                // from the ponded water left after evaporation, so the two
+                // losses never exceed the water available
+                infil = infilGetInfil(ctx, i, precip, runon,
+                                      std::max(0.0, depth - surfEvap * dt), dt,
                                       local_infil, recovery_factor);
             }
 
